===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang|pejorative}} An obese or otherwise swollen ankle that blends into the calf without clear demarcation.
#* '''2001''', ''[[w:Shallow Hal|Shallow Hal]]'':
#*: Hey, all l’m saying is she’s got '''cankles''', for God’s sake. ''What?'' '''Cankles'''! She’s got no ankles. It’s like the calf merged with the foot, cut out the middleman.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|passage=The “'''cankle'''” (or the appearance of not having an ankle, but the calf of the leg just connecting to the foot) is a look that many women have and most could live without.|author=Jeff Smith|title=Posing for Portrait Photography: A Head-to-Toe Guide}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|passage=They’d pass me magazines and ask how my '''cankle''' recovery was progressing. They’re ankles, not '''cankles'''. I don’t have '''cankles'''!|author=Franz Wisner|title=Honeymoon with my Brother}}
#* '''2007''', ''Family Guy'', season 5, "Bill And Peter's Bogus Journey":
#*: Now that's a cankle! Where does the calf fat end and the ankle fat begin? Who knows, that's the fun!
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=13 September|title=Saturday Night Live|passage=Amy Poeler as Hillary Clinton: Stop saying I have '''cankles'''!}}

